  "identity": "Floating G-major lantern song for a warm midregister harmonica: dotted calls open into little descending answers, with one hopeful rising sixth in the refrain. Offbeat entries, small lower-neighbor scoops and deliberate breaths let the busy plucked bass carry the motion. The peak turns the call inside out rather than raising the whole tune; only one brief G5 appears. Play the short ornaments lightly, not as brass attacks; leave the written silences empty. Four-quarter bars throughout.",
